{"id":"NCT07282600","title":"A Study of Eloralintide (LY3841136) in Participants With Obesity or Overweight, and Type 2 Diabetes","official":"A Phase 3 Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Once Weekly Eloralintide in Adult Participants With Obesity or Overweight, and Type 2 Diabetes","summary":"The main purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy and safety of eloralintide compared with placebo for body weight reduction in participants with overweight or obesity and type 2 diabetes. Participation in the study will last about 75 weeks.","conditions":["Overweight","Obesity"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Eloralintide"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have type 2 diabetes\n* Are on stable treatment for type 2 diabetes for at least 90 days prior to screening\n* Have a BMI ≥ 27 kg/m2\n* Have a stable body weight (\\<5% body weight change) for 90 days prior to screening\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have a prior or planned surgical treatment for obesity (liposuction, cryolipolysis, or abdominoplasty allowed if performed \\>1 year before screening)\n* Have a prior or planned endoscopic procedure and/or device-based therapy for obesity (prior device-based therapy acceptable if device removal was more than 6 months prior to screening)\n* Have type 1 diabetes\n* Have taken any of the following antihyperglycemic medications within 90 days before screening:\n\n  * amylin analogs\n  * glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonists\n  * glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide/glucagon-like peptide-1 (GIP/GLP) receptor agonists, or\n  * insulin\n* Have had within 90 days prior to screening:\n\n  * heart attack\n  * stroke\n  * coronary artery revascularization\n  * unstable angina, or\n  * hospitalization due to congestive heart failure\n* Have a history or diagnosis of New York Heart Association Functional Classification Class IV congestive heart failure\n* Have taken medications or alternative remedies intended for weight loss within 90 days of screening","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":1035,"start":"2025-12-15","pcd":"2028-01","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","areas":["other"],"central":["Trial questions or participation questions: 1-877-CTLILLY (1-877-285-4559) or · 317-615-4559 · LillyTrials@Lilly.com","Physicians interested in becoming principal investigators please contact · clinical_inquiry_hub@lilly.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Birmingham Clinical Research","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35209","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"205-870-4343"},{"f":"Cullman Clinical Trials","city":"Cullman","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35055","s":"R","lat":34.1748,"lon":-86.8436,"c":"256-708-2826"},{"f":"Tucson Clinical Research Institute","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85712","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":""},{"f":"San Fernando Valley Health Institute","city":"Canoga Park","pr":"California","zip":"91304","s":"R","lat":34.2011,"lon":-118.5981,"c":"818-222-6868"},{"f":"AMCR Institute","city":"Escondido","pr":"California","zip":"92025","s":"R","lat":33.1192,"lon":-117.0864,"c":"760-466-1520"},{"f":"NorCal Medical Research, Inc","city":"Greenbrae","pr":"California","zip":"94904","s":"R","lat":37.9485,"lon":-122.5247,"c":"415-461-1585"},{"f":"Ark Clinical Research","city":"Long Beach","pr":"California","zip":"90815","s":"R","lat":33.767,"lon":-118.1892,"c":""},{"f":"Pacific Clinical Studies","city":"Los Alamitos","pr":"California","zip":"90720","s":"R","lat":33.8031,"lon":-118.0726,"c":"562-598-0600 ext 205"},{"f":"Inglewood Clinical","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90056","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"310-693-5000"},{"f":"Care Access - Santa Clarita","city":"Santa Clarita","pr":"California","zip":"91321","s":"R","lat":34.3917,"lon":-118.5426,"c":"661-371-7272"},{"f":"Encompass Cl